<request-parameters>
<!--
  D176 = "Provisional Mortality Statistics, 2018 through Last Month".
  Updated monthly. This is what lights up Causes of Death for 2021+
  (D76 stops at 2020).

  DRAFT — adapted from wonderapi's D176_Defaults.xml (its own accepted
  default envelope) plus the four edits that turn it into a
  "Year x 113-Cause-List, national, with rates" request, matching what
  mortality_icd10.xml (D76) does:

    B_2      *None*      -> D176.V4     (group by the ICD-10 113 Cause List)
    M_4      (added)     -> D176.M4     (age-adjusted rate)
    O_aar    aar_none    -> aar_std     (needed for M_4)
    O_ucd    D176.V2     -> D176.V4     (rank by the 113 list, not full ICD detail)
    F_D176.V1            -> {{YEAR_LIST}}  (fetch.js fills it; era clips to 2021+)
    O_show_totals true   -> false
    O_precision  1       -> 3

  UNVERIFIED: that D176's 113 Cause List is variable V4 (it is on D76).
  Test before trusting:
    cd pipeline
    node --env-file=.env fetch.js --type=mortality --era=provisional \
         --years=2021 --out=rows.json --dump
  Expect ~130 cause rows for 2021 with death_count / population /
  crude_rate / age_adjusted_rate populated. If rows.json instead has
  thousands of rows (individual ICD-10 codes) or is empty, V4 is wrong —
  paste the WONDER <message> from mortality_provisional.raw.xml, or the
  D176 variable list, and we'll re-point B_2 / O_ucd.

  When it validates: add an era to lib/datasets.js (databaseId 'D176',
  templateFile 'mortality_provisional.xml', fixed { icd_version: 10 },
  yearMin 2021, yearMax <current>, same 6-column contract as icd10) and
  a bullet in templates/README.md.
-->
